        "body": "Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis that develops when there is too much uric acid in the blood (hyperuricaemia). Uric acid is produced when the body breaks down purines â€” substances found naturally in the body and in many foods. When uric acid levels are too high, it can crystallise and deposit in joints as needle-like monosodium urate crystals, triggering intense inflammation and pain. Gout is more common in men and becomes increasingly common with age. It affects around 2.5% of the UK population.",
